        "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4(-\\frac{1}{4})x.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$",
